    memcpy(res, reply_data, nbytes);

    UnlockDisplay(dpy);
    SyncHandle();
    free(reply_data); // Free the partially allocated memory
    return res;
}
```

In this corrected version, we first calculate the total size of the reply by multiplying the length with 4 (since each byte is 4 bits). Then, we allocate memory of this size using `Xmalloc`. After copying the reply data into the allocated memory, we free the partially allocated memory using `free` to prevent memory leaks. This ensures that the program does not attempt to read beyond the allocated memory, thus mitigating the buffer overflow vulnerability.

