### Root Cause
The root cause of this vulnerability lies in the assumption that the length of the port number will always be less than or equal to the maximum allowed length. If the port number is longer than the maximum allowed length, it will cause an overflow when the `snprintf` call attempts to write beyond the allocated buffer.

