The function uses `find_first_bit` and `find_next_bit` to locate the first and next set bits in the bitmap, respectively. These functions assume that there is only one set bit per word. If there are multiple set bits per word, this can cause the loop to iterate over the same word multiple times, leading to an out-of-bounds access when accessing the `rq` pointer.

